	bdsk-url-1 = {http://gji.oxfordjournals.org/content/203/3/2237.abstract%20N2%20-%20We%20present%20a%20new%20grand%20mean%20palaeomagnetic%20pole%20(Plong:%20222.1%C2%B0,%20Plat:%20%E2%88%9264.0%C2%B0,%20A95:%202.6%C2%B0,%20N%20=%2049)%20for%20the%20ca.%201110%20Ma%20Umkondo%20large%20igneous%20province%20(LIP)%20of%20the%20Kalahari%20Craton.%20New%20palaeomagnetic%20data%20from%2024%20sills%20in%20Botswana%20and%20compiled%20reprocessed%20existing%20data%20are%20used%20to%20develop%20a%20palaeomagnetic%20pole%20as%20the%20Fisher%20mean%20of%20cooling%20unit%20virtual%20geomagnetic%20poles%20(VGPs).%20The%20mean%20and%20its%20associated%20uncertainty%20provide%20the%20best-constrained%20pole%20yet%20developed%20for%20the%20province.%20Comparing%20data%20from%20individual%20cooling%20units%20allows%20for%20evaluation%20of%20palaeosecular%20variation%20at%20this%20time%20in%20the%20Mesoproterozoic.%20The%20elongation%20of%20the%20population%20of%20VGPs%20is%20consistent%20with%20that%20predicted%20by%20the%20TK03.GAD%20model%20lending%20support%20to%20the%20dipolar%20nature%20of%20the%20field%20in%20the%20late%20Mesoproterozoic.%20In%20our%20new%20compilation,%204%20of%2059%20(%E2%88%BC7%20per%20cent)%20of%20the%20igneous%20units%20have%20northerly%20declinations%20while%20the%20rest%20are%20south-directed%20indicating%20that%20a%20geomagnetic%20reversal%20occurred%20during%20magmatic%20activity.%20Interpreting%20which%20of%20these%20polarities%20corresponds%20with%20a%20normal%20or%20reversed%20geomagnetic%20field%20relative%20to%20other%20continents%20can%20constrain%20the%20relative%20orientations%20between%20cratons%20with%20time-equivalent%20data.%20This%20interpretation%20is%20particularly%20important%20in%20comparison%20to%20Laurentia%20as%20it%20bears%20on%20Kalahari's%20involvement%20and%20position%20in%20the%20supercontinent%20Rodinia.%20The%20dominance%20of%20south-directed%20declinations%20within%20the%20Umkondo%20Province%20was%20previously%20used%20to%20suggest%20that%20these%20directions%20are%20the%20same%20polarity%20as%20reversed%20directions%20from%20the%20early%20magmatic%20stage%20of%20the%20Keweenawan%20Midcontinent%20Rift%20of%20Laurentia.%20Two%20Umkondo%20sills%20with%20northerly%20declinations%20have%20U-Pb%20baddeleyite%20ages%20of%20ca.%201109%20Ma%20that%20are%20temporally%20close%20to%20dated%20Midcontinent%20Rift%20units%20having%20reversed%20directions.%20Based%20on%20this%20comparison,%20and%20palaeomagnetic%20data%20from%20younger%20units%20in%20the%20Kalahari%20Craton,%20we%20favour%20the%20option%20in%20which%20the%20sites%20with%20northerly%20declinations%20from%20the%20Umkondo%20Province%20correspond%20to%20the%20reversed%20polarity%20directions%20from%20the%20early%20magmatic%20stage%20in%20the%20Midcontinent%20Rift.%20This%20interpretation%20allows%20for%20the%20Namaqua-Natal%20metamorphic%20belt%20of%20Kalahari%20to%20be%20a%20conjugate%20to%20the%20Grenville%20margin%20of%20North%20America%20and%20for%20Kalahari%20to%20have%20become%20conjoined%20with%20Laurentia%20within%20the%20supercontinent%20Rodinia%20subsequent%20to%20Umkondo%20LIP%20magmatic%20activity.}}

